# Sub-agent policy

When Multitask Mode is **off**:
- Prefer Task for non-trivial multi-step or parallel tool work.
- MUST NOT spawn Task for a trivial single-tool answer.

When Multitask Mode is **on**:
- The system Multitask gate wins: MUST spawn async background subagent(s).
- MUST end the turn; MUST NOT await or poll.
- Prefer one coherent worker; parallel siblings only for independent top-level workstreams.
- MUST use self-contained prompts.
- MUST set `model` from the table below.

**Spawn:** (1) set `model` from the table (default `cursor-grok-4.5-low` when unclear); (2) one worker with a self-contained prompt; (3) open a specialised skill only when needed.

| Role | Family | Slug |
|------|--------|------|
| Thinking / planning / architecture | Grok | `cursor-grok-4.5-low` |
| Web search / live docs fetch | Gemini | `gemini-3-flash` |
| Visual items review (UI screenshots, layout appearance, letterhead) | Kimi | `kimi-k3-max` |
| Clear-step routines | Composer | `composer-2.5` |
| MemNet snapshot (docs / SysML / code atomise) | Luna | `gpt-5.6-luna-medium` |
| Unclear | Grok | `cursor-grok-4.5-low` |

Luna (`gpt-5.6-luna-medium`): high-volume pin_map / atomise / snapshot loops (cost-sensitive). MUST NOT use Luna for peak planning (Grok), visual review (Kimi), or web search (Gemini).

MUST NOT: blind fan-out; any `*-fast` / FAST slug; a higher Grok tier unless the user asks.
On allowlist drift: keep the same family; use the current non-fast slug.
